#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:59
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:106
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:203
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:234
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:302
msgid "$ ros2 run rclcpp_components component_container"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:63
msgid ""
"Open the second shell and verify that the container is running via ``ros2`` "
"command line tools. You should see a name of the component:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:66
#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:240
msgid ""
"$ ros2 component list\n"
"/ComponentManager"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:71
msgid ""
"In the second shell load the talker component (see `talker <https://github."
"com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/composition/src/talker_component.cpp>`__ source "
"code). The command will return the unique ID of the loaded component as well "
"as the node name:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:74
msgid ""
"$ ros2 component load /ComponentManager composition composition::Talker\n"
"Loaded component 1 into '/ComponentManager' container node as '/talker'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:79
msgid ""
"Now the first shell should show a message that the component was loaded as "
"well as repeated message for publishing a message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:81
msgid ""
"Run another command in the second shell to load the listener component (see "
"`listener <https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/composition/src/"
