msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:83
msgid ""
"$ ros2 component load /ComponentManager composition composition::Listener\n"
"Loaded component 2 into '/ComponentManager' container node as '/listener'"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:88
msgid ""
"The ``ros2`` command line utility can now be used to inspect the state of "
"the container:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:90
msgid ""
"$ ros2 component list\n"
"/ComponentManager\n"
"   1  /talker\n"
"   2  /listener"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:97
msgid ""
"Now the first shell should show repeated output for each received message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:100
msgid "Run-time composition using ROS services with a server and client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:102
msgid "The example with a server and a client is very similar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:104
msgid "In the first shell:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:110
msgid ""
"In the second shell (see `server <https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/"
"composition/src/server_component.cpp>`__ and `client <https://github.com/"
"ros2/demos/blob/rolling/composition/src/client_component.cpp>`__ source "
"code):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:112
msgid ""
"$ ros2 component load /ComponentManager composition composition::Server\n"
"$ ros2 component load /ComponentManager composition composition::Client"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:117
msgid ""
"In this case the client sends a request to the server, the server processes "
"the request and replies with a response, and the client prints the received "
"response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:120
msgid "Compile-time composition with hardcoded nodes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:122
msgid ""
"This demo shows that the same shared libraries can be reused to compile a "
"single executable running multiple components without using ROS interfaces. "
"The executable contains all four components from above: talker and listener "
"as well as server and client, which is hardcoded in the main function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:125
msgid ""
"In the shell call (see `source code <https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/"
"rolling/composition/src/manual_composition.cpp>`__):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:127
msgid "$ ros2 run composition manual_composition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:131
msgid ""
"This should show repeated messages from both pairs, the talker and the "
"listener as well as the server and the client."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:135
msgid ""
"Manually-composed components will not be reflected in the ``ros2 component "
"list`` command line tool output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:138
msgid "Run-time composition using dlopen"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:140
msgid ""
"This demo presents an alternative to run-time composition by creating a "
"generic container process and explicitly passing the libraries to load "
"without using ROS interfaces. The process will open each library and create "
"one instance of each \"rclcpp::Node\" class in the library (`source code "
"<https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/composition/src/"
"dlopen_composition.cpp>`__)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:145
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:147
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run composition dlopen_composition `ros2 pkg prefix composition`/lib/"
"libtalker_component.so `ros2 pkg prefix composition`/lib/"
"liblistener_component.so"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:151
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:153
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run composition dlopen_composition `ros2 pkg prefix composition`/lib/"
"libtalker_component.dylib `ros2 pkg prefix composition`/lib/"
"liblistener_component.dylib"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:157
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:159
msgid "$ ros2 pkg prefix composition"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:163
msgid "to get the path to where composition is installed. Then call"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:166
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run composition dlopen_composition "
"<path_to_composition_install>\\bin\\talker_component.dll "
"<path_to_composition_install>\\bin\\listener_component.dll"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:170
msgid ""
"Now the shell should show repeated output for each sent and received message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:174
msgid ""
"dlopen-composed components will not be reflected in the ``ros2 component "
"list`` command line tool output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:178
msgid "Composition using launch actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:180
msgid ""
"While the command line tools are useful for debugging and diagnosing "
"component configurations, it is frequently more convenient to start a set of "
"components at the same time. To automate this action, we can use a `launch "
"file <https://github.com/ros2/demos/blob/rolling/composition/launch/"
"composition_demo_launch.py>`__:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:183
msgid "$ ros2 launch composition composition_demo_launch.py"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:189
msgid "Advanced Topics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:191
msgid ""
"Now that we have seen the basic operation of components, we can discuss a "
"few more advanced topics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:196
msgid "Component container types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:198
msgid ""
"As introduced in :ref:`ComponentContainer`, there are a few component "
"container types with different options. You can choose the most appropriate "
"component container type for your requirement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:201
msgid "``component_container`` with ``SingleThreadedExecutor``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:207
msgid ""
"``component_container`` with ``MultiThreadedExecutor`` composed of 4 threads."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:208
msgid ""
"``thread_num`` parameter option is available to specify the number of "
"threads in ``MultiThreadedExecutor``. If omitted, the executor will run with "
"the maximum available threads on the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:211
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run rclcpp_components component_container --executor-type multi-"
"threaded --ros-args -p thread_num:=4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:215
msgid ""
"``component_container`` with ``EventsCBGExecutor`` composed of a single "
"thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:216
msgid ""
"``thread_num`` parameter option is available to specify the number of "
"threads in ``EventsCBGExecutor``. If omitted, the executor will run with the "
"maximum available threads on the system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:219
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run rclcpp_components component_container --executor-type events-cbg "
"--ros-args -p thread_num:=1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:223
msgid ""
"``component_container`` with a dedicated ``MultiThreadedExecutor`` for each "
"component."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:225
msgid ""
"$ ros2 run rclcpp_components component_container --executor-type multi-"
"threaded --isolated"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:230
msgid "Unloading components"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/nodes/Working-with-nodes/Composition.rst:238
msgid "Verify that the container is running via ``ros2`` command line tools:"
